/-!
# Fi22 Schreier-edge words and their checking interface

Each candidate word is a product of already certified commuting-conjugate
subgroup entries. Base-32 digits encode a table index and an inverse flag.
GAP factor order is reversed for Lean multiplication. Truncation or erroneous
data cannot establish membership: the checks still compare the resulting
actual group element with the literal edge on all 48 faithful coordinates.

Source: ATLAS F22G1-p3510B0; GLS3 Table 5.3t and its conjugation-action paragraph.
Regenerate the candidate words with `source/generate.py`.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Fischer.Fi22.TransvectionComparison.Generation.Edges
open KernelCertificate SmallBase

def entry (n : Nat) : Entry :=
  (if n < 7 then (if n < 3 then (if n < 1 then entry00 else (if n < 2 then entry01 else entry02)) else (if n < 5 then (if n < 4 then entry03 else entry04) else (if n < 6 then entry05 else entry06))) else (if n < 11 then (if n < 9 then (if n < 8 then entry07 else entry08) else (if n < 10 then entry09 else entry10)) else (if n < 13 then (if n < 12 then entry11 else entry12) else (if n < 14 then entry13 else entry14))))

def decodeWord : Nat → Nat → List (Entry × Bool)
  | 0, _ => []
  | fuel + 1, code =>
    if code = 0 then [] else
      (entry ((code % 32 - 1) / 2), code % 2 == 0) :: decodeWord fuel (code / 32)

